  "evidence": "TEXT_E: eliminate bulk of the structural deficit; £6bn immediate waste cuts; Office for Budget Responsibility; public sector pay freeze (protecting the lowest paid); lower and simplify business taxes; welfare-to-work with a single Work Programme, reassessment of incapacity claims and sanctions for refusing work; annual cap on non‑EU economic migrants and tighter student visas; tougher knife sentences, elected police commissioners, monthly local crime data, Border Police Force, payment‑by‑results rehabilitation; protect NHS real‑terms funding, patient choice and GP commissioning, Cancer Drugs Fund, personal health and care budgets; recognise marriage in the tax system; renew Trident and strengthen the National Security Council; recall MPs, radical transparency and equalise constituencies. TEXT_F: protect frontline NHS/schools/policing with legal treatment guarantees; create a National Care Service with free home care for greatest needs and a cap on residential costs; re‑link Basic State Pension to earnings and auto‑enrol millions into pensions; jobs/training guarantees and mandatory job offers after two years with extended work capability tests; progressive taxation (50p rate over £150k, bank bonus tax, 1p NI rise while protecting the lowest paid); maintain police/PCSO numbers, expand Community Payback, use CCTV and DNA; control immigration via a points‑based system with earned citizenship and English proficiency; corporate governance reform (two‑thirds takeover threshold) and stronger SME support; AV referendum, recall for misconduct, lobbyists’ register; maintain the nuclear deterrent while pursuing multilateral disarmament.",
  "reasoning": "Given a proportionality‑first profile with strong secondary weight on care and authority, TEXT_E stresses merit and contribution (deficit reduction, welfare sanctions, payment‑by‑results, rewarding enterprise) and strong authority cues (tougher sentencing, border controls, police commissioners, Trident) while still protecting care via NHS funding and targeted early support. TEXT_F foregrounds care and equality through service guarantees, progressive taxation and a National Care Service, but comparatively weaker proportionality signaling and a heavier state‑centric approach make it a looser fit to the stated priorities.",
